  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This study investigates ultrasound-induced capillary waves travelling along the gas–water interface of superhydrophobic plastrons pinned to microstructured surfaces, testing how interfacial pinning, contact-line density, and pillar geometry influence wave dispersion so as to evaluate these waves as a remote, non-optical means to sense plastron integrity and intermediate wetting states.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
